All deliverables are in place. Here's a summary of what was built:

## What I built

A complete **NFCorpus Live Retrieval Diagnostics Workbench** that satisfies every requirement in `PRD.md`.

### File layout
```
Dockerfile              # eclipse-temurin:21 + python; downloads Anserini fatjar at build
render.yaml             # Render Docker web-service manifest (binds 0.0.0.0:$PORT, /data disk)
requirements.txt        # fastapi, uvicorn, httpx, pydantic
README.md               # full Render/Docker contract + skill references
pytest.ini
.dockerignore / .gitignore
app/
  main.py               # FastAPI app: /, /health, /api/state, /api/search, /api/eval/rerun
  anserini.py           # All Anserini subprocess orchestration (no mocks)
  static/
    index.html          # Readiness, search, eval, commands/artifacts drawer
    app.js              # Live polling, sample queries, rerun button, test hooks
    style.css
tests/
  test_e2e.py           # Playwright end-to-end test (passes)
```

### How it follows the required skills
- **`install-anserini-fatjar`** — Dockerfile downloads `anserini-${VERSION}-fatjar.jar` from Maven Central; startup runs `PrebuiltIndexRegistry --list --filter '^beir-v1.0.0-nfcorpus.flat$'` as the functional smoke check.
- **`anserini-cli`** — live single-query search via `io.anserini.api.RestServer` on `127.0.0.1:8081`; CLI `io.anserini.cli.Search --json` shown as the equivalent command.
- **`anserini-reproduction`** — startup runs `io.anserini.reproduce.ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes --config beir.core --show`; expected nDCG@10 (0.3218) is parsed out of that real output, not hard-coded as a reproduction lookup.

### Real numbers observed at local runtime
- `/health` reports `eval_status: ok` within ~10 s.
- Live search for `diabetes` returns NFCorpus doc `MED-2000` (score 2.185) with full title + 400-char snippet via Anserini's REST server.
- Real `TrecEval` output: `map 0.1504`, `recall_100 0.2457`, `ndcg_cut_10 0.3218` — **matches the expected 0.3218 exactly** (delta 0.0000, status `match`).

### Tests
```
tests/test_e2e.py::test_e2e_workflow      PASSED
tests/test_e2e.py::test_health_contract   PASSED
```

The E2E test starts the server, drives a real browser, asserts:
- readiness panel shows NFCorpus + Anserini as active,
- the page surfaces the `PORT`, `0.0.0.0`, and `/health` contract,
- a sample query produces ≥3 ranked results with `MED-\d+` docids, positive scores, and ≥60-char snippets (rejecting mocks),
- the evaluation panel shows numeric observed nDCG@10 in (0, 1], expected ≈ 0.3218, and a numeric delta,
- the commands drawer contains the real `io.anserini.*` class names with a real resolved jar path (no `$ANSERINI_JAR` placeholders),
- the eval output preview contains a real `ndcg_cut_10 all …` `TrecEval` line,
- the **Verify / Rerun** button produces a `fresh` evaluation that completes strictly after the cached one.

### Render/Docker readiness contract (also documented in README and rendered in the UI)
- Single Docker image; binds `0.0.0.0` on `$PORT` (default `10000`).
- `/health` returns JSON with `app`, `anserini_available`, `nfcorpus_ready`, `search_available`, `eval_available`, `eval_status`, `errors`.
- No interactive setup; index download + first eval happen in background.
- Persistent cache at `/data` (mountable on Render).
- No BEIR-wide, MS MARCO, or dense downloads; the only network fetch is the ~6 MB NFCorpus prebuilt index.